                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "This game is in essence a momentum-based platformer akin to the classic Sonic games while using real-world concepts and physics to innovate on the formula. The amount of liquid you have being a sort of health meter is simple yet ingenious -- the best kind of design. This core gameplay manages to remain engaging throughout the game's forty-eight levels, and to emphasize how fluid (pun intended) the movement of the liquid is, the game greatly encourages you to go fast in these levels. While some of the more gimmicky parts can be a bit frustrating at first, they also support speedy play in their own ways. Great little game overall, and while I feel it doesn't get enough recognition, I am glad people continue to review it on Steam to this day.",
